From 42c9039ea4ab6bd1c7d9db88d52b02dc963febd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:20:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] ASoC: wsa884x: balance pm_runtime_enable() with
 devm-managed disable

Every other resource acquired in wsa884x_probe() (regulators, reset
control) is devm-managed and unwound automatically on detach.
pm_runtime_enable() was the one exception, called as a bare function
call with no corresponding pm_runtime_disable() on teardown.

This is silent under a normal single-probe lifecycle, but
qcom_swrm_reprobe_unattached_slaves() (drivers/soundwire/qcom.c) can
force a second .probe() via device_reprobe() on any slave still stuck
at dev_num 0 after the enumeration retry budget. The forced detach
runs the devm cleanup for everything else, but never balances the
earlier pm_runtime_enable(), so the second successful probe enables
runtime PM a second time on an already-enabled device: "Unbalanced
pm_runtime_enable!", and that codec instance is left in a broken
runtime-PM state from then on -- silent on whichever channel it drives,
for the remainder of that boot.

Reproduced on an ASUS Zenbook A16 (UX3607OA): the SoundWire slave that
lost the enumeration race and needed the reprobe fallback showed this
warning and stayed non-functional, while its sibling on the same bus,
which attached cleanly on the first try, was unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
index a367c94bfb4d..b2edec2a448e 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -2038,6 +2038,11 @@ static int wsa884x_get_reset(struct device *dev, struct wsa884x_priv *wsa884x)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void wsa884x_pm_runtime_disable(void *data)
+{
+	pm_runtime_disable(data);
+}
+
 static int wsa884x_probe(struct sdw_slave *pdev,
 			 const struct sdw_device_id *id)
 {
@@ -2126,6 +2131,19 @@ static int wsa884x_probe(struct sdw_slave *pdev,
 	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * Every other resource acquired above is devm-managed and unwound on
+	 * detach. This one was not, so a forced device_reprobe() (see
+	 * drivers/soundwire/qcom.c: qcom_swrm_reprobe_unattached_slaves())
+	 * calls pm_runtime_enable() a second time on a device that was never
+	 * balanced by pm_runtime_disable() on the first detach, producing
+	 * "Unbalanced pm_runtime_enable!" and a codec left in a broken
+	 * runtime-PM state -- silent on that channel from then on.
+	 */
+	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, wsa884x_pm_runtime_disable, dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	return devm_snd_soc_register_component(dev,
 					       &wsa884x_component_drv,
 					       wsa884x_dais,
-- 
